    "_postman_id": "02f164fc-3248-4871-847b-4d05ead92841",
    "name": "Product Service API",
    "description": "# Product Service API\n\nIntegration tests for the **Product Service**, a thread-safe REST API built in Go with Gin, deployed to AWS ECS Fargate via Terraform.\n\n## Getting Started\n\nThis collection uses **Environment Variables** for switching between Local and AWS targets.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Import this collection into Postman.\n    \n2. Import the `Local` and `AWS` environments.\n    \n3. Select the appropriate environment from the top-right dropdown.\n    \n\n| Variable | Local | AWS |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `baseUrl` | `http://localhost:8080` | `http://<fargate-public-ip>:8080` |\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Health Check\n\n- **GET /health** - Returns `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` (200)\n    \n\n### Product Management\n\n- **POST /products/:id/details** - Creates a product (204 No Content)\n    \n- **GET /products/:id** - Retrieves product by ID (200)\n    \n\n### Error Cases\n\n- **GET /products/999** - Product not found (404)\n    \n- **GET /products/abc** - Invalid product ID (400)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "52400206",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/52400206-02f164fc-3248-4871-847b-4d05ead92841?source=collection_link"
  },
